The command line interface for building, serving, and shipping leptos apps.

Usage: leptoskit <COMMAND>

Commands:
  migrate      Upgrades leptoskit.toml to the current configuration schema
  native       Builds native application hosts and generates plugin registration
  test         Runs component and device tests with retained failure artifacts
  device       Controls attached devices, apps, and websites: list, boot, drive, and inspect them, one command or one JSON document at a time
  mcp          Serves the device control API over the Model Context Protocol, on standard input and output or over HTTP
  rpc          Describes the published RPC and generates clients for it
  generate     Generates an application, a runtime plugin crate, or a tooling plugin program
  new          Scaffolds a new project
  dev          Runs every platform you have set up, and rebuilds them on change
  build        Builds the project for a platform
  serve        Serves the built output
  routes       Writes the typed `Route` module from the routes directory
  l10n         Writes the typed translations module from the ARB files in the locales directory
  db           Writes and applies database migrations from the app's `#[db::table]` structs
  codepush     Manages code push releases
  doctor       Checks the local environment for missing tooling; exits non-zero when a required check fails
  format       Formats Rust, and the markup in `view!` macros, with the project's `rustfmt.toml`
  lint         Checks the project with the leptoskit rules and clippy, side by side
  completions  Generates shell completions
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version
